body:
**Shape.** The transfer marker on a borrow right-hand side is accepted, and the new binding `a` is treated as owned: at scope end the object is disposed through `a` and through its owner `b`.

```bezel
module Probe;

public sealed class Q
  private _id: int;
  public constructor(id: int)
    _id := id;
  end constructor;
  destructor
    Console.WriteLine($"D:{_id}");
  end destructor;
  public method Use()
    Console.WriteLine($"U:{_id}");
  end Use;
end Q;

public sealed class R
  private _id: int;
  public owned f: Q;
  public constructor(id: int, owned q: Q)
    _id := id;
    f := q;
  end constructor;
  destructor
    Console.WriteLine($"D:{_id}");
  end destructor;
  public method Use()
    Console.WriteLine($"U:{_id}");
  end Use;
  public static method Take(owned r: R)
    using var k := move r;
  end Take;
  public static method Body()
    var b := new R(2, new Q(1));
    var c := b;                       // c borrows b
    var a := move c;                  // `move` on a borrow: a spelling error per §28.3.7; accepted
    a.Use();
  end Body;
end R;

public class Program
  public static method Main(): int
    R.Body();
    Console.WriteLine("END");
    return 0;
  end Main;
end Program;
```

**Measured on r35.** Compiles with zero diagnostics in both modes. `--checked-disposal`: `U:2 D:2 D:1 END`, exit 0 (the second disposal is the idempotent no-op on the set flag, so checked mode hides it). `--unchecked-disposal`: `U:2 D:2 D:1` then **SIGSEGV** (exit 139) — the second release frees the block again.

The same acceptance with a *field* borrow: `var a := new R(new Q()); var c := a.f; var b := move c;` compiles clean and disposes `Q#1` through `b` before `a`'s cascade reaches it (`D:1 D:2` in checked mode; SIGSEGV unchecked).

**Spec (v0.345).** §28.3.7 *Move semantics for owned locals*: *"Three spelling errors follow, mirroring the call-site marker's rules: the marker on a **borrow or fresh-producer right-hand side**; …"* — K3.4 (§28.3.1) lists the marked binding transfer `var y := move x;` for an **owned binding** only; a borrow has no obligation to transfer (K1.2). Expected: a compile error at `move c` naming the borrow. Code-generation reference §4.2: *"`move` is also an error on a borrow"*.

**Differential numbers.** 30 of 6,000 sampled programs (pins + temps fragments, vars 3 / len 4) and 38 of 6,000 (fields + try/while) carry this shape; all are accepted by r35 and rejected by the model as `K3-consume-of-non-owned`; every one crashes in unchecked mode when the double release is reached.

**Measured on r35** (`bezelc 0.0.0-f6863e62`, the 2026-10-27 release build; main may have moved since). Found by the model-vs-compiler differential (`scratch/bzdiff`, proposal 0047 §5.3 / soundness README §3.2): the executable ownership model (bzcore L1, spec v0.345) and `bezelc` disagree on this program; the model's verdict is the spec's sentence quoted above.
